1
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,040
First ranger, you have command of Castle Black.

2
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:06,490
Lord Commander, it is my duty to tell you

3
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:09,870
I believe this mission to be reckless, foolhardy,

4
00:03:09,870 --> 00:03:11,730
and an insult to all the brothers

5
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:14,210
who have died fighting the wildlings.

6
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:17,130
As always, thank you for your honesty.

7
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,250
Safe travels, Lord Commander.

8
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,440
Thank you, Sam.

9
00:03:35,850 --> 00:03:37,280
It's dragonglass.

10
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:39,470
It's what I used to kill the white walker.

11
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,140
I hope you don't need them.

12
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:49,080
Me, too.

13
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,520
There he is.

14
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,840
That laugh.

15
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,030
Egg.

16
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:34,980
Egg laughed like that.

17
00:04:35,610 --> 00:04:38,580
One of the first things I remember.

18
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:45,940
His little brother Aegon. He became king.

19
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:51,790
And before that, he was a jolly fellow,

20
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:53,380
like this one.

21
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:02,050
Get him south, gillyflower.

22
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:06,120
Before it's too late.

23
00:05:57,020 --> 00:05:58,320
Theon, wait.

24
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:00,730
Not Theon, my lady. Reek.

25
00:06:00,930 --> 00:06:02,050
Help me.

26
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:06,210
You're his wife now.

27
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,420
Theon.

28
00:06:08,690 --> 00:06:10,000
Do what he says.

29
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,880
Do what he says or he'll hurt you.

30
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,930
He already hurts me every night.

31
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:15,960
All day I'm locked in this room

32
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,730
And every night he comes...

33
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:22,090
It can't be any worse.

34
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:26,120
It can. It can always be worse.

35
00:06:35,170 --> 00:06:37,050
- What did he do to you? - Please.

36
00:06:37,050 --> 00:06:39,630
- You betrayed my family! - I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

37
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:42,130
You have to help me. Theon, help me.

38
00:06:42,130 --> 00:06:44,180
He'll see us. You don't know him.

39
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:47,070
My family still has friends in The North.

40
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:49,830
All I need to do is give a signal and they'll rescue me.

41
00:06:50,310 --> 00:06:52,370
Climb to the top of the broken tower.

42
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,850
Light this candle and put it in the window.

43
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:57,730
- Promise me, Theon. - Reek! My name is Reek.

44
00:07:00,350 --> 00:07:03,080
Your name is Theon Greyjoy.

45
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:06,900
Last surviving son of Balon Greyjoy,

46
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,330
Lord of the Iron Islands.

47
00:07:08,330 --> 00:07:09,600
Do you hear me?

48
00:07:12,770 --> 00:07:13,810
Theon...

49
00:07:16,330 --> 00:07:17,550
Promise me.

50
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,480
Yes, Reek?

51
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:39,550
Egg.

52
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:42,410
Egg.

53
00:08:45,170 --> 00:08:47,370
Mother's looking for you.

54
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,320
Egg.

55
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:54,620
Get some sleep, Sam.

56
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,950
You'll have to speak for him tomorrow.

57
00:08:59,670 --> 00:09:01,290
You don't know that.

58
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:02,680
Get some sleep.

59
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:05,490
I'll watch over him.

60
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,100
I'm staying, too.

61
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:13,030
He's always been good to me.

62
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:15,010
I can't leave him now.

63
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,130
Egg!

64
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,590
Egg.

65
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:34,680
I dreamed...

66
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:37,580
that I was old.

67
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:51,220
His name was Aemon Targaryen.

68
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:54,400
He came to us from King's Landing.

69
00:09:56,690 --> 00:09:59,610
A maester of the citadel, chained and sworn,

70
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:02,920
and sworn brother of the night's watch, ever faithful.

71
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:06,280
No man was wiser

72
00:10:06,790 --> 00:10:10,190
or gentler or kinder.

73
00:10:11,610 --> 00:10:14,700
At the wall, a dozen Lord Commanders

74
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:17,100
came and went during his years of service,

75
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:19,300
but he was always there to counsel them.

76
00:10:22,510 --> 00:10:24,070
He was the blood of the dragon...

77
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:28,210
But now his fire has gone out.

78
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:32,910
And now his watch is ended.

79
00:10:33,310 --> 00:10:35,740
And now his watch is ended.

80
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,460
You're losing all your friends, Tarly.

81
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:45,870
My beautiful wife.

82
00:11:51,950 --> 00:11:53,710
When my father told me we were marrying,

83
00:11:53,710 --> 00:11:56,950
I half expected a fat, bearded beast.

84
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:04,530
Do you know how pleased I was when I saw you?

85
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:06,590
You've made me very happy.

86
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:14,990
Our scouts report that Stannis Baratheon rides for Winterfell.

87
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:16,750
He's a respected commander.

88
00:12:17,890 --> 00:12:21,530
His troops are loyal and battle-tested.

89
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:25,040
He's hired thousands of foreign sellswords to bolster his army.

90
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:28,510
But this storm is a stroke of luck for us northerners.

91
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,950
Our people are used to fighting in the frost.

92
00:12:34,730 --> 00:12:37,820
His army is out there now suffering in the snow.

93
00:12:39,650 --> 00:12:41,550
One day I'll be Lord of Wnterfell

94
00:12:41,550 --> 00:12:43,240
and warden of the North.

95
00:12:43,830 --> 00:12:46,330
You'll be my lady and Wardeness.

96
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:51,710
But isn't your stepmother pregnant?

97
00:12:51,850 --> 00:12:53,180
What of it?

98
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:56,250
What happens if she has a boy?

99
00:12:57,750 --> 00:12:59,570
Then I'll have a baby brother.

100
00:12:59,690 --> 00:13:01,240
But he'll be the heir.

101
00:13:01,250 --> 00:13:03,400
I'm Lord Bolton's eldest son.

102
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,440
But you're a bastard.

103
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:08,040
A trueborn will always have the stronger claim.

104
00:13:10,970 --> 00:13:13,570
I've been naturalized by a royal decree from...

105
00:13:13,570 --> 00:13:17,050
Tommen baratheon? Another Bastard.

106
00:13:23,590 --> 00:13:25,850
Bastards can rise high in the world.

107
00:13:26,890 --> 00:13:29,780
Like your half-brother Jon Snow.

108
00:13:30,930 --> 00:13:32,650
Born the bastard of Winterfell,

109
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:36,740
now the Lord Commander of the Night's Watch.

110
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:40,160
You didn't know?

111
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:43,600
Yes, he's done very well for himself.

112
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:48,260
I nearly forgot why I asked you to join me.

113
00:13:48,810 --> 00:13:50,050
Come, my lady.

114
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:03,370
Your northern friend.

115
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:08,390
Reek told me you wanted to leave.

116
00:14:09,630 --> 00:14:10,610
Why?

117
00:14:11,150 --> 00:14:12,440
Winterfell is your home

118
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,100
and I am your husband.

119
00:14:15,210 --> 00:14:16,660
Tough old bird.

120
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:19,750
Everyone talks when I start peeling them.

121
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,190
But this one,

122
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:24,820
her heart gave out before I even got to her face.

123
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:30,100
We do breed them tough in the North.

124
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:38,070
Bring my wife back to her chamber.

125
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:41,180
It's far too cold out here for a lady.

126
00:14:41,970 --> 00:14:44,170
You should hold on to your candles.

127
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:47,430
The nights are so long now.

128
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:39,190
40 horses died in the night.

129
00:15:40,430 --> 00:15:42,330
We'll lose more come sunset.

130
00:15:42,550 --> 00:15:43,830
We're running out of food.

131
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:46,440
We can't open the supply line until the snow clears.

132
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:53,170
What else?

133
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,860
The Stormcrows rode off last night.

134
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:00,670
500 men.

135
00:16:04,290 --> 00:16:05,660
Sellswords.

136
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,740
Loyal to nothing but gold.

137
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:14,790
We still have a hard march to Winterfell

138
00:16:14,790 --> 00:16:16,980
and we won't be marching anywhere in this weather.

139
00:16:17,610 --> 00:16:18,230
And?

140
00:16:18,390 --> 00:16:20,130
This isn't our time.

141
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:23,530
We should head back to Castle Black when the snow clears.

142
00:16:23,530 --> 00:16:25,930
I retreated from King's Landing, Ser Davos.

143
00:16:25,930 --> 00:16:29,530
If I retreat again, I'll become the king who ran.

144
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:31,460
- Your grace... - Winter is coming.

145
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:34,610
Those aren't just the Stark words. It's a fact.

146
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:37,290
If we march back to Castle Black,

147
00:16:37,810 --> 00:16:39,650
we winter at Castle Black.

148
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:43,720
And who can say how many years this winter will last?

149
00:16:43,730 --> 00:16:45,840
It's better to wait for the right time than risk everything.

150
00:16:45,850 --> 00:16:48,160
This is the right time and I will risk everything.

151
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:50,810
Because if I don't, we've lost.

152
00:16:51,430 --> 00:16:53,250
We march to victory

153
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:57,120
or we march to defeat.

154
00:16:57,530 --> 00:16:59,920
But we go forward. Only forward.

155
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:11,550
Your grace.

156
00:17:16,770 --> 00:17:18,560
I've trusted in your visions

157
00:17:19,210 --> 00:17:22,250
and your prophecies for years.

158
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:24,080
You saw it yourself, my king,

159
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:26,540
when you stared into the flames.

160
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:28,430
A great battle in the snow.

161
00:17:28,430 --> 00:17:30,510
- I don't know what I saw. - You do know.

162
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,040
Trust yourself.

163
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:34,100
And you? Do you trust yourself?

164
00:17:34,810 --> 00:17:36,270
I trust in the Lord.

165
00:17:38,690 --> 00:17:40,380
Are you sure?

166
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:50,210
I have seen myself walk along the battlements of Winterfell.

167
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:54,930
I have seen the flayed man banners lowered to the ground.

168
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:07,300
But sometimes sacrifices must be made to ensure victory.

169
00:18:09,470 --> 00:18:11,880
I have shown you the power of king's blood.

170
00:18:12,810 --> 00:18:14,770
The usurper Robb Stark.

171
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,730
The usurper Joffrey Baratheon.

172
00:18:16,730 --> 00:18:19,020
We don't have Robert's bastard here.

173
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:22,060
No, we have someone better.

174
00:18:23,990 --> 00:18:26,430
And your blood runs through her veins.

175
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,140
Have you lost your mind?

176
00:18:30,170 --> 00:18:31,450
Do you doubt me?

177
00:18:31,970 --> 00:18:33,210
Still?

178
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,260
After all that you've seen.

179
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,680
There must be another way.

180
00:18:37,860 --> 00:18:40,390
- Leeches or... - There is only one way.

181
00:18:40,850 --> 00:18:44,110
You must become king before the long night begins.

182
00:18:44,110 --> 00:18:46,600
Only you can lead the living against the dead.

183
00:18:46,630 --> 00:18:49,600
All your life has led us to this moment.

184
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:52,100
- To this decision. - She's my daughter.

185
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,140
Get out.

186
00:19:18,730 --> 00:19:20,540
There's always some sort to grub on.

187
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:22,200
A bit of mutton would be nice.

188
00:19:25,930 --> 00:19:27,530
A beauty from beyond the wall.

189
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:33,050
Where you going, love? Aren't we better-looking than the fat man?

190
00:19:33,050 --> 00:19:35,790
No, the question is is she pretty down south in the real world

191
00:19:35,790 --> 00:19:38,030
or is she pretty 'cause she's the only girl here?

192
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:40,120
Even in White Harbor, I'd want a kiss.

193
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:42,940
Come on, love, give us a kiss.

194
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:44,580
- Leave me alone. - Oh, if you were my girl,

195
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:45,720
I wouldn't leave you alone.

196
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,730
- One little kiss. - Come on, give him a kiss.

197
00:19:47,730 --> 00:19:49,330
A man gets lonely guarding the wall.

198
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:55,850
There's no need to be rude.

199
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,950
We just want a little affection.

200
00:20:01,930 --> 00:20:03,210
Get your hands off her.

201
00:20:03,930 --> 00:20:06,810
Brother Derek, Brother Brant,

202
00:20:06,810 --> 00:20:08,770
I believe you both have guard duty tonight.

203
00:20:08,770 --> 00:20:09,930
Sam the slayer.

204
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:11,850
You gonna slay me with that sword?

205
00:20:11,850 --> 00:20:12,890
Look at his hand shake.

206
00:20:13,270 --> 00:20:15,400
Gilly, go on.

207
00:20:15,690 --> 00:20:17,700
Get back to your room, lock the door.

208
00:20:20,890 --> 00:20:23,800
- I'm warning you. - Come on. Come on.

209
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:28,820
Sam!

210
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:32,060
You lying sack of shit.

211
00:20:32,470 --> 00:20:34,000
Killed a white walker, eh?

212
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:35,850
You fat-ass fuck.

213
00:20:36,850 --> 00:20:37,830
Come on, get up.

214
00:20:38,390 --> 00:20:41,320
- No! - This your hero? This hog?

215
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,120
Leave him alone!

216
00:20:44,190 --> 00:20:46,680
Stubborn little wildling bitch, aren't you?

217
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:50,110
- Come on! - No!

218
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:54,060
- Sam! Sam! Sam! - Come on!

219
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:04,870
- Sam! Sam! - Come on.

220
00:21:04,870 --> 00:21:05,850
Right.

221
00:21:07,150 --> 00:21:08,840
I'll deal with this.

222
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:12,880
- Turn her over. - All right.

223
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:18,790
I said get your hands off her.

224
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:20,320
You're gonna get yourself killed.

225
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:23,010
Your lover Jon Snow's not here to save you.

226
00:21:23,010 --> 00:21:25,520
I killed a white walker, I killed a Thenn.

227
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:28,070
I'll take my chances with you.

228
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:46,010
Sam!

229
00:21:48,550 --> 00:21:50,610
- I'm all right. - You're not.

230
00:21:51,170 --> 00:21:52,650
Just a bit woozy.

231
00:22:17,850 --> 00:22:20,610
The next time you see something like that, you leave it alone.

232
00:22:20,610 --> 00:22:23,170
I will not. They would have--

233
00:22:26,610 --> 00:22:28,110
I don't know what they would have done.

234
00:22:28,650 --> 00:22:31,260
I know they would have killed you if Ghost hadn't come.

235
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:34,230
No. No, no. They were tiring out.

236
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:37,140
I had them in the palm of my hand.

237
00:22:38,010 --> 00:22:40,190
Don't be stupid, Sam.

238
00:22:40,590 --> 00:22:42,200
You're not a fighter.

239
00:22:43,310 --> 00:22:45,160
What kind of man would I be if I ran away

240
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:47,420
when I saw someone hurting you?

241
00:22:47,450 --> 00:22:49,500
Just promise me

242
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:53,170
whatever happens, you'll take care of little Sam.

243
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:54,850
But of course I will.

244
00:22:55,570 --> 00:22:56,520
And...

245
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:59,660
I'll take care of you, too.

246
00:23:06,370 --> 00:23:07,830
I need more water.

247
00:23:11,710 --> 00:23:12,790
Stay.

248
00:23:14,190 --> 00:23:15,350
Please?

249
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:17,110
Am I hurting you?

250
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:23,320
Are you sure?

251
00:24:53,300 --> 00:24:54,600
Oh, my!

252
00:25:11,850 --> 00:25:14,730
A rare find for the fighting pits, my friends.

253
00:25:15,250 --> 00:25:18,640
Not your usual street tough or drunken pirate.

254
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:22,230
This one's a Westerosi knight

255
00:25:22,230 --> 00:25:26,250
from an ancient house trained in sword and lance.

256
00:25:26,490 --> 00:25:28,990
He fought beside the Stag King Robert

257
00:25:28,990 --> 00:25:31,040
on the far side of the narrow sea.

258
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:34,240
He was first through the breach during the siege of Spike,

259
00:25:34,450 --> 00:25:37,610
slaughtering 50 men with his flaming sword.

260
00:25:38,150 --> 00:25:42,170
He killed the great Khal Drogo in single combat.

261
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:44,230
Betrayed by his woman,

262
00:25:44,230 --> 00:25:47,740
he sold himself into slavery to repay his debts.

263
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:51,150
Bidding begins at 12 gold honors.

264
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:55,050
13. Do I have 14?

265
00:25:55,820 --> 00:25:59,720
15? 15 gold honors.

266
00:25:59,720 --> 00:26:02,740
Do I hear 16? 16?

267
00:26:02,740 --> 00:26:03,890
20.

268
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:05,550
Sold.

269
00:26:15,570 --> 00:26:18,370
Wait! You have to buy me as well.

270
00:26:19,190 --> 00:26:20,090
Why?

271
00:26:20,750 --> 00:26:21,870
We're a team.

272
00:26:22,370 --> 00:26:23,870
I'm a great fighter, too.

273
00:26:27,770 --> 00:26:30,020
He's funny. You have to give him that.

274
00:26:40,780 --> 00:26:43,540
Stop! Stop!

275
00:26:57,340 --> 00:26:59,930
You're right, he's funny.

276
00:27:07,120 --> 00:27:08,970
Thank you, my lord. Thank you.

277
00:27:08,970 --> 00:27:09,870
Yes.

278
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:12,330
My lord, if I may.

279
00:27:12,490 --> 00:27:14,800
I've heard Meereen has become a free city.

280
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:15,740
You might run into trouble

281
00:27:15,740 --> 00:27:17,760
if you try to fight slaves in the fighting pits.

282
00:27:17,760 --> 00:27:20,170
Now, if you were to fight freed men who'd be paid a wage--

283
00:27:23,430 --> 00:27:25,210
There's your wages, funny man.

284
00:27:25,590 --> 00:27:27,330
Should last the rest of your life.

285
00:27:29,300 --> 00:27:32,210
These are warrior hands, not a serving girl's.

286
00:27:32,570 --> 00:27:34,150
5, going once...

287
00:27:38,450 --> 00:27:41,840
How long before the king of Meereen comes to claim my pillow?

288
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:43,330
Don't be ridiculous.

289
00:27:43,860 --> 00:27:47,090
My marriage to Hizdahr is political.

290
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:50,140
I think he's smart enough to understand that.

291
00:27:51,560 --> 00:27:53,640
I think the sons of the Harpy have stopped killing

292
00:27:53,640 --> 00:27:55,730
because their leader was made king.

293
00:27:58,940 --> 00:28:00,610
Are you jealous?

294
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:03,700
You think I'm petty enough to speak ill of a man

295
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:05,780
just because he represents competition?

296
00:28:06,990 --> 00:28:08,020
I do.

297
00:28:10,380 --> 00:28:11,410
You're right.

298
00:28:11,770 --> 00:28:14,730
My motivations are entirely impure.

299
00:28:23,260 --> 00:28:24,670
Doesn't make me wrong.

300
00:28:29,570 --> 00:28:33,830
You told me yourself I can't fight enemies within and without.

301
00:28:33,830 --> 00:28:36,090
So when enemies without come knocking,

302
00:28:36,380 --> 00:28:38,570
I need the city of Meereen behind me.

303
00:28:38,570 --> 00:28:39,880
I have no choice.

304
00:28:40,940 --> 00:28:42,440
Everyone has a choice.

305
00:28:42,590 --> 00:28:44,330
Even slaves have a choice...

306
00:28:44,330 --> 00:28:45,850
death or slavery.

307
00:28:46,580 --> 00:28:48,890
So what else can I do, hmm?

308
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,820
Marry me instead.

309
00:28:54,340 --> 00:28:58,190
Even if I wanted to do such an inadvisable thing,

310
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:00,710
I couldn't.

311
00:29:00,830 --> 00:29:01,840
Why not?

312
00:29:02,100 --> 00:29:04,320
You are queen. You can do what you like.

313
00:29:06,380 --> 00:29:09,750
No, I can't.

314
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:12,740
Then you are the only person in Meereen who's not free.

315
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:26,370
And I know I'm here to serve my queen

316
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:27,820
and not give advice,

317
00:29:28,820 --> 00:29:30,690
but can I make one more suggestion?

318
00:29:34,800 --> 00:29:36,030
Of course.

319
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:41,490
On the day of the great games,

320
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:44,870
gather all the great masters and wise masters

321
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:46,930
and worthy masters you can find

322
00:29:48,390 --> 00:29:49,980
and slaughter them all.

323
00:29:53,420 --> 00:29:57,040
I am a queen, not a butcher.

324
00:30:01,730 --> 00:30:04,530
All rulers are either butchers or meat.

325
00:30:13,630 --> 00:30:16,990
You there. Where would I find the High Septon

326
00:30:16,990 --> 00:30:20,940
or High Sparrow or whatever bloody fool name he's got?

327
00:30:21,060 --> 00:30:24,640
It's not as good a name as Queen of Thorns, I'll admit.

328
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:27,890
You should have the decency

329
00:30:27,920 --> 00:30:30,210
to stand when you speak to a lady.

330
00:30:30,280 --> 00:30:33,030
You should have the decency to kneel before the gods.

331
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:34,870
Don't spar with me, little fellow.

332
00:30:37,870 --> 00:30:40,470
For me, it's the knees.

333
00:30:40,850 --> 00:30:42,970
- You? - Hips.

334
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:48,240
A man of the people. Is that your game?

335
00:30:48,780 --> 00:30:52,520
It's an old game. Dull and unconvincing.

336
00:30:52,590 --> 00:30:54,020
A man of the people

337
00:30:54,530 --> 00:30:57,590
who does Cersei's dirty work for her.

338
00:30:58,470 --> 00:31:00,360
The people always do the dirty work.

339
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:01,470
Spare me the homilies.

340
00:31:01,550 --> 00:31:03,870
I can smell a fraud from a mile away.

341
00:31:03,870 --> 00:31:04,980
Useful talent.

342
00:31:04,980 --> 00:31:08,050
I'm here for my grandson and granddaughter.

343
00:31:08,050 --> 00:31:10,170
Your grandson and granddaughter

344
00:31:10,180 --> 00:31:12,960
swore sacred vows and lied.

345
00:31:13,700 --> 00:31:16,140
The Father judges us all.

346
00:31:16,390 --> 00:31:18,240
Sons of high lords,

347
00:31:18,750 --> 00:31:20,190
Sons of fishermen.

348
00:31:20,690 --> 00:31:23,960
If you break his laws, you will be punished.

349
00:31:25,040 --> 00:31:26,630
Don't you walk away from me.

350
00:31:26,640 --> 00:31:28,820
You don't give commands here, Lady Olenna.

351
00:31:28,830 --> 00:31:30,220
What is it you want?

352
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:32,010
Gold?

353
00:31:32,570 --> 00:31:35,430
I'll make you the richest septon who ever lived.

354
00:31:36,900 --> 00:31:38,100
What, then?

355
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:41,520
I imagine this is strange for you.

356
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:44,650
Everyone you meet has a hidden motive

357
00:31:44,650 --> 00:31:47,650
and you pride yourself on sniffing it out.

358
00:31:48,660 --> 00:31:50,680
But I'm telling you a simple truth.

359
00:31:51,140 --> 00:31:52,610
I serve the gods.

360
00:31:52,910 --> 00:31:55,100
The gods demand justice.

361
00:31:55,100 --> 00:31:57,470
How do they communicate their demands?

362
00:31:57,800 --> 00:31:59,210
By raven or horse?

363
00:31:59,210 --> 00:32:01,790
By the holy text, "The seven-pointed star."

364
00:32:02,460 --> 00:32:04,970
If you don't have one in your library,

365
00:32:04,970 --> 00:32:05,870
I'll give you my own.

366
00:32:05,880 --> 00:32:08,510
I've read "The seven-pointed star."

367
00:32:08,510 --> 00:32:10,440
Then you'll remember the passages

368
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:13,110
concerning buggery and perjury.

369
00:32:13,230 --> 00:32:15,280
Your grandchildren will be punished

370
00:32:15,280 --> 00:32:17,610
in the same manner as anyone

371
00:32:17,610 --> 00:32:19,850
who breaks the sacred laws.

372
00:32:19,850 --> 00:32:21,380
Half the men, women, and children

373
00:32:21,380 --> 00:32:24,840
in this foul city break the sacred laws.

374
00:32:25,180 --> 00:32:28,350
You live among murderers, thieves, and rapists,

375
00:32:28,350 --> 00:32:33,650
and yet you punish Loras for shagging some perfumed ponce

376
00:32:33,770 --> 00:32:36,130
and Margaery for defending her brother?

377
00:32:36,130 --> 00:32:40,800
Yes. The gods' laws must be applied to all equally.

378
00:32:41,050 --> 00:32:43,300
If it's equality you want, so be it.

379
00:32:43,300 --> 00:32:47,330
When House Tyrell stops sending our crops to the capital,

380
00:32:47,660 --> 00:32:49,540
everyone here will starve.

381
00:32:50,280 --> 00:32:52,840
And I'll make sure the hungry know who's to blame.

382
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:58,450
Have you ever sowed the field, Lady Olenna?

383
00:33:00,490 --> 00:33:02,280
Have you ever reaped the grain?

384
00:33:03,990 --> 00:33:05,800
Has anyone in House Tyrell?

385
00:33:07,010 --> 00:33:08,570
A lifetime of wealth and power

386
00:33:08,570 --> 00:33:10,800
has left you blind in one eye.

387
00:33:12,650 --> 00:33:16,630
You are the few, we are the many.

388
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:21,760
And when the many stop fearing the few...

389
00:33:36,140 --> 00:33:37,270
Lady Olenna.

390
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:53,210
Starving yourself won't make things any better for her, my love.

391
00:33:56,460 --> 00:33:58,110
She's in a prison cell

392
00:33:58,590 --> 00:34:01,370
and there is nothing I can do.

393
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,400
I am the King!

394
00:34:06,550 --> 00:34:10,000
The Queen is in prison and there is nothing I can do!

395
00:34:24,290 --> 00:34:25,980
No matter who you are,

396
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:29,730
no matter how strong you are, sooner or later,

397
00:34:29,730 --> 00:34:32,360
you'll face circumstances beyond your control.

398
00:34:33,020 --> 00:34:35,360
Events you couldn't possibly have anticipated

399
00:34:35,360 --> 00:34:37,220
or prevented even if you had.

400
00:34:37,430 --> 00:34:39,630
You cannot blame yourself for fate.

401
00:34:40,520 --> 00:34:41,700
Your father,

402
00:34:43,070 --> 00:34:44,560
Your brother, your grandfather--

403
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:47,370
I was Queen of the Seven Kingdoms and what could I do?

404
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:49,870
Hold them as they left this world.

405
00:34:50,590 --> 00:34:52,490
Kissed their heads after they'd gone.

406
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:54,510
I'll call in the army.

407
00:34:54,890 --> 00:34:56,920
I'll take back the Sept

408
00:34:56,920 --> 00:35:00,530
and kill every last one of them.

409
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:04,780
I'll start a war if I have to.

410
00:35:04,780 --> 00:35:05,860
You know as well as I do

411
00:35:05,860 --> 00:35:08,300
who the first casualty of that war would be.

412
00:35:13,340 --> 00:35:14,510
I love her.

413
00:35:18,270 --> 00:35:19,560
I love her...

414
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:24,190
And I can't help her.

415
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:41,810
We must be strong for those we love.

416
00:35:41,810 --> 00:35:43,780
We cannot give in to despair.

417
00:35:44,410 --> 00:35:46,850
I will speak with the High Sparrow.

418
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:48,570
There must be something he--

419
00:35:48,570 --> 00:35:50,340
Let me talk to him on your behalf.

420
00:35:51,350 --> 00:35:55,270
The king cannot sully himself negotiating with an unwashed fanatic.

421
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:58,550
You will try to help her?

422
00:35:58,690 --> 00:36:02,000
I'll do everything I can to win her freedom and her brother's.

423
00:36:02,100 --> 00:36:04,560
Your happiness is all I want in this world.

424
00:36:06,010 --> 00:36:08,820
- I know. - No, you don't.

425
00:36:12,540 --> 00:36:14,220
You can't possibly.

426
00:36:16,140 --> 00:36:18,080
Not until you have children of your own.

427
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:21,110
I would do anything for you.

428
00:36:23,310 --> 00:36:25,390
Anything to keep you from harm.

429
00:36:27,830 --> 00:36:30,110
I would burn cities to the ground.

430
00:36:31,950 --> 00:36:33,570
You are all that matters.

431
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:39,280
You and your sister.

432
00:36:39,770 --> 00:36:42,000
From the moment you came into this world.

433
00:36:42,840 --> 00:36:44,060
My boy.

434
00:36:47,100 --> 00:36:48,470
My only boy.

435
00:37:04,370 --> 00:37:05,820
Prince Doran hopes this satisfies

436
00:37:05,820 --> 00:37:08,350
your concerns about the princess's well-being.

437
00:37:15,680 --> 00:37:17,270
You looked different when I left.

438
00:37:17,700 --> 00:37:20,210
You had more hair.

439
00:37:20,210 --> 00:37:21,600
And more hands.

440
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:25,890
- How's Trystane? - He'll be all right.

441
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,030
I'm sorry for that.

442
00:37:27,030 --> 00:37:28,700
It wasn't supposed to happen that way.

443
00:37:28,830 --> 00:37:30,440
Why is it happening at all?

444
00:37:31,620 --> 00:37:33,370
Your mother's worried about you.

445
00:37:35,340 --> 00:37:36,760
Threats have been made.

446
00:37:36,860 --> 00:37:38,490
Dorne's too dangerous for you.

447
00:37:38,490 --> 00:37:40,650
- I've come to take you home. - This is my home.

448
00:37:40,650 --> 00:37:42,160
This has been my home for years.

449
00:37:42,160 --> 00:37:44,730
I didn't want to come here, but she told me to.

450
00:37:44,730 --> 00:37:45,710
I did what she said.

451
00:37:45,710 --> 00:37:48,530
I did my duty and now she's forcing me to go back?

452
00:37:48,530 --> 00:37:51,650
It's for your own good. These are complicated matters.

453
00:37:51,650 --> 00:37:53,950
No, it's not complicated at all. It's simple.

454
00:37:53,950 --> 00:37:56,430
I love Trystane, I'm going to marry him,

455
00:37:56,430 --> 00:37:57,880
and we're staying right here.

456
00:37:57,880 --> 00:38:00,170
- I don't understand. - Of course you don't.

457
00:38:00,170 --> 00:38:01,460
You don't know me.

458
00:38:10,170 --> 00:38:14,450
*Brothers, oh brothers, my days here are done,*

459
00:38:14,460 --> 00:38:18,970
*the Dornishman's taken my life,*

460
00:38:19,010 --> 00:38:23,800
*But what does it matter, for all men must die,*

461
00:38:23,810 --> 00:38:27,400
*and I've tasted the Dornishman's wife!*

462
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:34,760
*I've tasted the Dornishman's wife!*

463
00:38:36,620 --> 00:38:38,260
He's got a good voice.

464
00:38:39,220 --> 00:38:40,870
We're lucky he's a singer.

465
00:38:40,950 --> 00:38:43,600
If he were a fighter, we might have been in trouble.

466
00:38:44,340 --> 00:38:46,390
It's against my code to hurt a woman.

467
00:38:46,390 --> 00:38:47,140
It's amazing

468
00:38:47,150 --> 00:38:49,550
how many men we beat seem to have this code.

469
00:38:49,550 --> 00:38:51,300
I wouldn't say you beat me.

470
00:38:51,870 --> 00:38:53,090
How's your arm?

471
00:38:53,090 --> 00:38:54,250
Wonderful.

472
00:38:55,260 --> 00:38:58,070
Wouldn't feel right to leave Dorne without a new scar.

473
00:38:58,630 --> 00:39:00,340
You think you're leaving Dorne?

474
00:39:00,540 --> 00:39:01,850
No great hurry.

475
00:39:02,330 --> 00:39:05,370
Dornish women are the most beautiful women in the world.

476
00:39:05,620 --> 00:39:06,560
Thank you.

477
00:39:06,560 --> 00:39:09,860
I said Dornish women. I didn't say you.

478
00:39:12,210 --> 00:39:15,010
I'm not the most beautiful woman you've ever seen?

479
00:39:16,270 --> 00:39:19,640
I've seen quite a few women in all the seven kingdoms.

480
00:39:19,850 --> 00:39:22,890
Name one more beautiful than I am.

481
00:39:24,630 --> 00:39:28,040
Well, now, in King's Landing,

482
00:39:28,170 --> 00:39:31,320
there was an absolutely gorgeous...

483
00:39:35,950 --> 00:39:37,300
There was a what?

484
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:42,130
In King's Landing, you were saying?

485
00:39:42,870 --> 00:39:44,030
Was I?

486
00:39:45,320 --> 00:39:47,860
There was a woman more beautiful than I am.

487
00:39:48,050 --> 00:39:49,130
Was there?

488
00:39:49,830 --> 00:39:51,800
My memory's not what it was earlier.

489
00:39:55,580 --> 00:39:56,920
How's your arm now?

490
00:39:57,200 --> 00:39:59,060
You seem concerned with it.

491
00:39:59,060 --> 00:40:00,750
You must really like me.

492
00:40:09,390 --> 00:40:12,180
And how about your head?

493
00:40:16,850 --> 00:40:18,000
My head?

494
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:20,350
My head?

495
00:40:21,580 --> 00:40:24,040
You don't even want to know what's going on in--

496
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:36,330
Your nose is bleeding.

497
00:40:39,470 --> 00:40:42,030
It's nothing. It's the dry air.

498
00:40:45,710 --> 00:40:49,590
My dagger was coated with a special ointment from Asshai.

499
00:40:50,070 --> 00:40:52,000
They call it the Long Farewell.

500
00:40:52,560 --> 00:40:54,090
It takes time to work,

501
00:40:54,700 --> 00:40:58,400
but if a single drop makes contact with the skin,

502
00:40:58,890 --> 00:40:59,990
death.

503
00:41:08,190 --> 00:41:10,260
The only antidote.

504
00:41:15,130 --> 00:41:17,630
Who's the most beautiful woman in the world?

505
00:41:18,970 --> 00:41:19,980
You.

506
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:23,710
Sorry? Who?

507
00:41:26,280 --> 00:41:27,400
You.

508
00:41:28,950 --> 00:41:30,130
Don't drop it.

509
00:41:45,130 --> 00:41:47,200
I think you're very handsome as well.

510
00:42:32,140 --> 00:42:34,800
- I'm sorry about the locale. - No, you're not.

511
00:42:37,470 --> 00:42:39,060
It felt like the safest place.

512
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:41,650
Not for your clientele, clearly.

513
00:42:42,450 --> 00:42:44,680
It was an establishment like no other.

514
00:42:46,030 --> 00:42:48,300
The sheer range of appetites catered to.

515
00:42:48,300 --> 00:42:52,480
Desires that didn't even exist until we invented them.

516
00:42:53,030 --> 00:42:56,340
You've always been rather impressed with yourself, haven't you?

517
00:42:57,590 --> 00:42:59,350
The past is the past.

518
00:43:00,430 --> 00:43:03,620
The future is all that's worth discussing.

519
00:43:05,340 --> 00:43:07,040
The future of House Tyrell.

520
00:43:07,040 --> 00:43:09,700
Don't pretend to have any concern for my house,

521
00:43:09,700 --> 00:43:11,680
my grandchildren or me.

522
00:43:11,990 --> 00:43:14,050
I should have known you'd return to the capital

523
00:43:14,050 --> 00:43:16,640
as soon as things started to go wrong.

524
00:43:16,640 --> 00:43:19,040
- I promise you-- - I promise you, Lord Baelish,

525
00:43:19,320 --> 00:43:21,200
that our fates are joined.

526
00:43:21,200 --> 00:43:22,900
Together we murdered a king.

527
00:43:23,200 --> 00:43:26,430
If my house should fall, I will have nothing to hide.

528
00:43:27,480 --> 00:43:31,050
And if I should meet with some accident

529
00:43:31,050 --> 00:43:33,960
here at your broken little flesh market,

530
00:43:34,460 --> 00:43:37,210
they'll never even find what's left of you.

531
00:43:38,320 --> 00:43:39,270
So...

532
00:43:40,360 --> 00:43:42,450
do you deny a part in all this?

533
00:43:42,630 --> 00:43:45,260
Cersei summoned me to King's Landing.

534
00:43:45,900 --> 00:43:47,270
I dared not refuse her.

535
00:43:47,270 --> 00:43:49,140
And what did she want?

536
00:43:49,140 --> 00:43:51,770
A piece of information she knew that I had.

537
00:43:52,270 --> 00:43:55,260
Neither silence nor lies were an option.

538
00:43:56,090 --> 00:43:57,760
But I have other information

539
00:43:58,580 --> 00:44:00,170
of which she is unaware.

540
00:44:01,450 --> 00:44:04,350
And as you say, our interests are aligned.

541
00:44:06,420 --> 00:44:07,750
I have a gift for you.

542
00:44:08,380 --> 00:44:10,060
What kind of gift?

543
00:44:10,100 --> 00:44:11,960
The same kind I gave Cersei.

544
00:44:13,530 --> 00:44:15,080
A handsome young man.

545
00:44:29,180 --> 00:44:31,630
Many worthy fighters have died

546
00:44:31,630 --> 00:44:34,120
trying to make it to the great games.

547
00:44:34,360 --> 00:44:35,330
When most of you worthless

548
00:44:35,330 --> 00:44:37,370
scum join them in death this afternoon,

549
00:44:37,370 --> 00:44:40,460
it will represent a significant rise in your station.

550
00:44:40,810 --> 00:44:43,530
But if you do happen to triumph here,

551
00:44:43,630 --> 00:44:46,260
you will fight at the great Pit of Daznak itself

552
00:44:46,260 --> 00:44:47,840
in front of the Queen.

553
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:52,080
So whatever happens, the gods have smiled upon you today.

554
00:44:52,560 --> 00:44:56,630
This is the day your lives actually start to mean something.

555
00:44:58,990 --> 00:45:01,830
You and you. You.

556
00:45:03,600 --> 00:45:04,470
You two.

557
00:45:06,690 --> 00:45:08,330
You, you, and you.

558
00:45:09,540 --> 00:45:10,430
Up.

559
00:45:11,750 --> 00:45:14,390
- Valar morghulis. - Valar dohaeris.

560
00:45:14,510 --> 00:45:16,190
Prepare yourselves.

561
00:45:28,710 --> 00:45:31,130
Sitting through the great games will be bad enough.

562
00:45:31,130 --> 00:45:34,120
For generations in the days leading up to the great games,

563
00:45:34,120 --> 00:45:35,890
it has been customary for our ruler

564
00:45:35,890 --> 00:45:37,630
to make the rounds of the lower pits

565
00:45:37,640 --> 00:45:40,600
to pay the fighters there the honor of her presence.

566
00:45:45,240 --> 00:45:46,510
Move yourselves.

567
00:45:53,320 --> 00:45:54,530
Your grace.

568
00:45:55,040 --> 00:45:56,430
Your future grace.

569
00:45:56,780 --> 00:45:58,150
You honor us all.

570
00:46:01,270 --> 00:46:02,600
Stand there.

571
00:46:03,540 --> 00:46:05,790
Stand straight. That's the fucking Queen.

572
00:46:07,580 --> 00:46:09,600
We fight and die for your glory,

573
00:46:09,680 --> 00:46:11,060
glorious Queen.

574
00:46:14,180 --> 00:46:16,370
We fight and die for your glory,

575
00:46:16,370 --> 00:46:18,290
glorious Queen.

576
00:46:20,230 --> 00:46:22,910
Fight!

577
00:47:20,940 --> 00:47:22,100
I think I've seen enough.

578
00:47:22,100 --> 00:47:25,000
Your grace, it is a tradition

579
00:47:25,110 --> 00:47:27,950
for the Queen to stay until the victor has emerged.

580
00:47:27,950 --> 00:47:30,430
I've sacrificed more than enough for your traditions.

581
00:47:35,550 --> 00:47:36,460
What are you doing?

582
00:47:45,890 --> 00:47:48,310
Wait your turn, you piece of fucking filth.

583
00:49:17,590 --> 00:49:19,020
Get him out of my sight.

584
00:49:19,410 --> 00:49:21,030
Khaleesi, please.

585
00:49:21,380 --> 00:49:23,200
I just need a moment of your time.

586
00:49:24,170 --> 00:49:25,550
I brought you a gift.

587
00:49:26,480 --> 00:49:27,430
It's true.

588
00:49:29,680 --> 00:49:30,670
He has.

589
00:49:32,440 --> 00:49:33,310
Who are you?

590
00:49:35,250 --> 00:49:36,390
I am the gift.

591
00:49:39,330 --> 00:49:41,160
It's a pleasure to meet you, your grace.

592
00:49:43,030 --> 00:49:44,880
My name isTyrion Lannister.

593
00:50:18,500 --> 00:50:20,060
This is horrible.

594
00:50:20,210 --> 00:50:21,590
Unacceptable.

595
00:50:23,800 --> 00:50:25,980
Are they feeding you enough at least?

596
00:50:27,560 --> 00:50:30,430
I brought you this. Venison.

597
00:50:31,340 --> 00:50:32,600
It's quite good.

598
00:50:35,840 --> 00:50:38,680
I had it myself for supper only last night.

599
00:50:42,840 --> 00:50:44,020
We did everything we could

600
00:50:44,020 --> 00:50:45,940
from the moment they took your brother.

601
00:50:46,130 --> 00:50:47,900
Tommen even went to the Sept himself

602
00:50:47,900 --> 00:50:49,690
to confront the High Sparrow.

603
00:50:50,510 --> 00:50:53,200
But I fear the Faith has left reason behind.

604
00:50:53,420 --> 00:50:55,710
I know you did this.

605
00:50:56,740 --> 00:51:00,010
We are making every effort on your behalf.

606
00:51:00,460 --> 00:51:02,810
I swear to you by all the seven gods.

607
00:51:02,810 --> 00:51:05,090
Lies come easily to you.

608
00:51:05,100 --> 00:51:06,720
Everyone knows that.

609
00:51:06,930 --> 00:51:08,580
But innocence,

610
00:51:09,540 --> 00:51:11,820
decency, concern,

611
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:14,770
you're not very good at those, I'm afraid.

612
00:51:16,330 --> 00:51:18,590
Perhaps that's why your son was so eager

613
00:51:18,600 --> 00:51:20,830
to cast you aside for me.

614
00:51:22,750 --> 00:51:24,170
You're upset.

615
00:51:24,990 --> 00:51:26,670
You're not thinking clearly.

616
00:51:27,260 --> 00:51:29,520
I'll visit again when you've had a chance to calm down.

617
00:51:29,520 --> 00:51:31,570
I don't want to see you again.

618
00:51:31,630 --> 00:51:34,030
I do hope you change your mind about that.

619
00:51:34,520 --> 00:51:36,530
I've been told men often go mad

620
00:51:36,530 --> 00:51:38,830
in the black cells beneath the Red Keep.

621
00:51:39,180 --> 00:51:40,980
Though I suppose your isolation will end

622
00:51:40,980 --> 00:51:42,780
when your trial begins.

623
00:51:44,590 --> 00:51:45,980
Leave.

624
00:51:46,450 --> 00:51:47,300
Yes.

625
00:51:48,440 --> 00:51:49,850
I'm afraid I must.

626
00:51:49,850 --> 00:51:51,970
My son needs me now more than ever.

627
00:51:52,570 --> 00:51:54,530
Get out, you hateful bitch!

628
00:52:08,730 --> 00:52:10,140
Sleep well, sister.

629
00:52:38,630 --> 00:52:39,740
Thank you, Boake.

630
00:52:47,060 --> 00:52:48,790
- You saw her? - Yes.

631
00:52:49,050 --> 00:52:51,320
- And? - Her accommodations seem sufficient.

632
00:52:51,320 --> 00:52:52,640
What happens to her now?

633
00:52:54,030 --> 00:52:56,060
Well, she and her brother are both being held

634
00:52:56,060 --> 00:52:57,720
under fair suspicion.

635
00:52:58,140 --> 00:53:00,650
A trial will be held for each of them

636
00:53:00,650 --> 00:53:03,490
to determine if they're guilty of any acts

637
00:53:03,490 --> 00:53:07,330
that might constitute a violation of the tenets of the faith.

638
00:53:07,620 --> 00:53:09,040
Who will stand judge?

639
00:53:09,040 --> 00:53:13,730
Seven septons as it was in all trials before the Targaryens.

640
00:53:14,800 --> 00:53:16,090
Will you be one of them?

641
00:53:16,570 --> 00:53:17,430
I will.

642
00:53:19,960 --> 00:53:21,720
If one or both of them

643
00:53:21,720 --> 00:53:24,110
were to confess before the trial...

644
00:53:24,130 --> 00:53:26,220
Then they will be shown the Mother's mercy.

645
00:53:27,520 --> 00:53:29,640
And what does the Mother's mercy entail?

646
00:53:30,420 --> 00:53:32,430
It depends upon the situation.

647
00:53:32,900 --> 00:53:35,680
The acts themselves, the degree of contrition.

648
00:53:35,680 --> 00:53:37,740
Thank you, High Septon,

649
00:53:38,590 --> 00:53:41,450
for bringing them whatever justice they deserve

650
00:53:42,400 --> 00:53:43,890
in the eyes of the Seven.

651
00:53:48,480 --> 00:53:49,690
Did you know this chapel

652
00:53:49,690 --> 00:53:52,620
is one of the oldest structures in King's Landing?

653
00:53:54,220 --> 00:53:56,240
I think I may have heard at one point.

654
00:53:56,580 --> 00:53:59,040
Baelor built his Sept around it.

655
00:54:00,740 --> 00:54:03,320
But men worshipped here long before him.

656
00:54:04,320 --> 00:54:06,180
Who carved this altar?

657
00:54:07,020 --> 00:54:09,210
- Do you know? - I'm afraid I don't.

658
00:54:10,490 --> 00:54:11,640
No one does.

659
00:54:12,530 --> 00:54:16,100
There's no name on it or anywhere else in the chapel.

660
00:54:18,320 --> 00:54:20,480
No, the people who built this place

661
00:54:20,700 --> 00:54:24,440
didn't inflict their vanity on those who came after them

662
00:54:24,840 --> 00:54:28,710
the way Baelor did with that great gilded monstrosity up there.

663
00:54:30,400 --> 00:54:32,180
Their faith was clean.

664
00:54:33,730 --> 00:54:36,810
Strip away the gold and the ornaments,

665
00:54:37,260 --> 00:54:39,670
knock down the statues and the pillars,

666
00:54:40,510 --> 00:54:42,270
and this is what remains.

667
00:54:45,450 --> 00:54:48,090
Something simple...

668
00:54:51,180 --> 00:54:54,830
and solid and true.

669
00:54:59,120 --> 00:55:02,270
The Tyrells' finery will be stripped away.

670
00:55:03,460 --> 00:55:05,300
Their lies knocked down.

671
00:55:05,300 --> 00:55:08,170
Their true hearts laid bare for all to see.

672
00:55:09,860 --> 00:55:11,970
And so it will be for all of us.

673
00:55:12,590 --> 00:55:15,020
High and low alike.

674
00:55:19,410 --> 00:55:20,920
What will we find

675
00:55:21,780 --> 00:55:24,210
when we strip away your finery?

676
00:55:27,810 --> 00:55:30,680
A young man came to us not long ago.

677
00:55:31,730 --> 00:55:33,900
Broken in body and spirit.

678
00:55:36,190 --> 00:55:38,610
He had so much to strip away.

679
00:55:40,370 --> 00:55:42,450
So much weighing him down.

680
00:55:44,090 --> 00:55:47,310
But piece by piece, he unburdened himself.

681
00:55:48,710 --> 00:55:50,230
Let go of vanity,

682
00:55:50,800 --> 00:55:53,110
pride, sin.

683
00:55:55,820 --> 00:55:58,070
Now his soul is so light,

684
00:55:58,500 --> 00:56:01,710
he will float through the Seven Heavens like a bird.

685
00:56:08,640 --> 00:56:10,830
And he has much to say about you.

686
00:56:35,220 --> 00:56:36,200
Move.

687
00:56:39,190 --> 00:56:41,690
Let me go immediately.

688
00:56:42,220 --> 00:56:44,590
You will order her to let me go.

689
00:56:44,710 --> 00:56:47,060
I am the queen! I am the queen!

690
00:56:47,060 --> 00:56:48,810
Have you lost your mind?

691
00:56:49,520 --> 00:56:50,800
Let me go!

692
00:56:52,620 --> 00:56:54,340
Get your filthy hands off me!

693
00:56:54,340 --> 00:56:56,060
Have you lost your mind?

694
00:56:56,890 --> 00:56:59,680
I am the queen! Let me go!

695
00:57:06,040 --> 00:57:06,950
Look at me.

696
00:57:10,120 --> 00:57:11,550
Look at my face.

697
00:57:14,490 --> 00:57:17,330
It's the last thing you'll see before you die.

